<article class="env-exercise" id="0CSZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CSZ">Exercise <span data-tag="0CSZ">111.12.5</span>.</a> Let $(R, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. Show that there exists a canonical short exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to K \to M \to Q \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> such that the following are true </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\text{depth}(Q) \geq 1$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$K$ is zero or $\text{Supp}(K) = \{ \mathfrak m\} $, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{length}_ R(K) < \infty $. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Hint: using the Noetherian property show that there exists a maximal submodule $K$ as in (2) and then show that $Q = M/K$ satisfies (1) and $K$ satisfies (3). </p>
</article>